\title{ForestFireR: Spatial and Mean-Field Forest-Fire Invasion Model}
\description{
Simulation of a two-species vegetation system in which fire mediates the
competition between a native species and an invader, on an explicit
lattice or in its well-mixed limit. The engine is written in C++ and
exposed to R through Rcpp.
}
\details{
See \link{ForestFireR-model} for the definition of the model: states,
transitions, parameters and the mean-field equations.

To run it: \code{\link[=generate_landscape]{generate_landscape()}} builds an initial spatial
configuration, \code{\link[=simulate_spatial]{simulate_spatial()}} runs the lattice Gillespie
simulation, \code{\link[=simulate_mean_field]{simulate_mean_field()}} integrates the deterministic
well-mixed limit and \code{\link[=simulate_mean_field_stochastic]{simulate_mean_field_stochastic()}} simulates the
well-mixed stochastic process at a finite population size.
\code{\link[=default_rates]{default_rates()}} gives the baseline parameter set and \code{\link[=xi2lambda]{xi2lambda()}}
converts the dimensionless spread/regrowth probabilities into rate
constants. \code{\link[=generate_landscape_layers]{generate_landscape_layers()}} and
\code{\link[=simulate_spatial_from_grid]{simulate_spatial_from_grid()}} cover initial conditions that
\code{\link[=generate_landscape]{generate_landscape()}} cannot express, and \code{\link[=simulate_spatial_movie]{simulate_spatial_movie()}}
renders a run as a video.

